  "caseId": "case17",
  "description": "PF3 is not a cancel key in this program. The second arm of the EVALUATE EIBAID at app/cbl/COUSR02C.cbl:111-119 performs UPDATE-USER-INFO FIRST and only then returns, so the pending edit is SAVED on the way out - the opposite of what PF3 does in most CICS applications, and a behaviour a redesign would be tempted to 'correct'.\n\nThe first name changes from RAYMOND to RAY, so one change test fires, the rewrite succeeds and two sends occur. Then, because CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM is 'COUSR00C' rather than blank, the ELSE at :116-117 moves it into CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM and RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN transfers there.\n\nThe termination is XCTL, not RETURN_TRANSID, and the two are not interchangeable: XCTL transfers control and never comes back, so the EXEC CICS RETURN at :135-138 is not reached on this path. RETURN-TO-PREV-SCREEN also rewrites three commarea fields - CDEMO-FROM-TRANID to 'CU02', CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM to 'COUSR02C' and CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT to zero - and the navigation below states all three, because the commarea travels in the payload and is carried into the next transaction.",
